WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.935
Day one is a check, not a lesson.

2
00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:04.026
It shows you where the reading sticks.

3
00:00:04.726 --> 00:00:09.157
You hold the grown-up page. Your child reads from the page with the big words.

4
00:00:09.607 --> 00:00:10.785
There are three parts.

5
00:00:11.235 --> 00:00:18.181
Part A. Your child reads the ten words. Mark a word only if it is said all at once, with no sounding out loud.

6
00:00:18.631 --> 00:00:23.298
This is sounding out loud. It gets no check mark, even when the word is right.

7
00:00:26.354 --> 00:00:27.389
The word is cat.

8
00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:32.872
All at once means your child looks, and just says the word. That gets a check mark.

9
00:00:33.322 --> 00:00:36.038
If a word is read wrong, put an X in its box.

10
00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:43.436
Part B. Four sentences, made of the same ten words. Mark a sentence if no word in it was sounded out loud.

11
00:00:43.886 --> 00:00:50.397
Part C. One long sentence. Your child reads it once. Then you ask the question printed on your page.

12
00:00:50.847 --> 00:00:55.634
Then mark what was true. Did the words come in groups? Did the voice go down at the end?

13
00:00:56.084 --> 00:01:00.113
Did your child keep their place to the end? And could they answer your question?

14
00:01:00.563 --> 00:01:05.175
Do not teach, do not correct, and do not use a timer. Just listen and mark.

15
00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:11.342
Then read the yellow box at the bottom of your page, from the top. Stop at the first line that fits.

16
00:01:11.792 --> 00:01:16.320
That line names the most likely sticking point, and tells you which days matter most.

17
00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:21.448
Write the three numbers on the page, and keep it. You will look at it again on the last day.
